        "procedure": "Under argon (Schlenk/glovebox), a cold (-40 °C) solution of HL (294.9 mg, 1.11 mmol, 2 eq.) in DME (4 mL) was added to a stirring solution of [Yb(HMDS)2(THF)2] (355.8 mg, 0.56 mmol, 1 eq.) in DME (2 mL). The orange solution was stirred overnight at -40 °C. Solvent was removed under vacuum to give an orange powder. The solid was dissolved in cold n-hexane (3 mL), stirred at -40 °C for 15 min and dried; this recrystallization/drying cycle was repeated three times to remove coordinated DME (heating under vacuum was avoided because it causes decomposition). The solution was filtered and concentrated. Storage at -40 °C yielded green crystals of 1-Yb.",
